This paper studies time series tokenization in time series forecasting, which is an interesting and important issue in time series analytics. Overall, the reviewers’ comments are mainly on the negative side, with complaints on 
- experiments: data sets, baselines, statistical signifcance of the results; 
- method assumption: justification on the first-order Markov assumption;
- related work: other adaptive, non-fixed-size patching approaches, such as LightGTS (ICML 25). This line of research is totally ignored;  

I take into account the author feedback, but still feel that addressing all the issues from the reviewers need substantial work, which perhaps needs a new round of review. This prevents the paper to be accepted at this current form.
